      "content": "My bad, I forgot I need to upload the raw data files first. I'm attaching the scan summary and the pigment profile report now. \n\n[FILE ATTACHED: scan_summary_landscape_04.pdf]\n[FILE ATTACHED: pigment_profile_report.csv]\n\nOkay, so the report is pretty clear: the binder shows significant traces of a synthetic polymer that didn't exist until the mid-19th century. Given the attribution is for a 1640s master, this is a massive red flag. But the provenance looks absolutely airtight, coming straight from a high-profile estate. Looking at both the scan data and the documentation, how do you weigh this discrepancy? Can we still justify the attribution despite the binder?",
